Fancyband is made of parts under different licenses. Each part's terms apply
to that part only.

engine/
    Angband 4.2.6 and Fancyband's changes to it. You may use it under either
    the GNU General Public License, version 2, or the "Angband licence", which
    allows use for educational, research, and not-for-profit purposes.
    See engine/docs/copying.rst and docs/licenses/GPL-2.0.txt.
    engine/FANCYBAND-CHANGES.md says what Fancyband changed, and how to find
    each change and its date.

engine/lib/tiles/, sounds, and fonts
    These have their own terms, listed in engine/docs/copying.rst. In short:
    Adam Bolt's tiles may be used for any purpose; David Gervais' are under
    Creative Commons Attribution 3.0; Shockbolt's may be used only with
    Angband and its variants, free of charge, and must not be changed.

client/, proto/, scripts/, and docs/
    Fancyband's own work, under the Apache License, version 2.0. See
    docs/licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.

Limoni
    The client builds a fork of Limoni, github.com/mmatis/limoni, under the
    Apache License, version 2.0. See docs/limoni-fork.md.

The engine and the client are separate programs that talk over a socket.
Do not link them into one binary: the GPL version 2 and the Apache License,
version 2.0, do not allow their code to be combined in one program.
